  "_age_bands_comment": "Coarse bands, used only to look up per-condition age_multipliers and to calibrate a per-band prevalence intercept. They are NOT the sampling distribution - see age_pyramid.",

  "age_pyramid": {
    "_comment": "The actual sampling distribution for patient age. Ages were previously drawn by picking one of the five coarse bands and then drawing uniformly inside it, which produced a flat slab of 27 identically-likely ages across 18-44 and an implausible cliff at each band edge. Real age distributions are smooth and, crucially, an EHR or claims extract is not a census: it over-represents whoever uses healthcare. share is the US Census 2020 population share; utilization is the relative annual encounter rate for that band. The sampler draws proportional to share x utilization, then uniformly within the 5-year band, which yields the correct three-humped shape - an infant bump from well-child visits, a trough through the healthy twenties, and a heavy tail after 65.",
