  "_facilities_comment": "case_mix multiplies the chance a patient with a condition in that grouper attends this facility, so an oncology institute's population really is enriched for cancer and its inpatient mix differs from a primary-care group's. coding_style drives per-facility documentation habits: how many diagnosis codes land on an encounter, how often the unspecified variant is chosen over a specific one, and how reliably the primary diagnosis is sequenced first. These are the idiosyncrasies that make multi-site harmonisation hard, and a dataset where every site codes identically cannot exercise that.",

  "network": {
    "_comment": "Patients were previously bound to exactly one facility for life, with the facility code baked into the MRN, so cross-site record linkage - the central problem in multi-site RWD - was impossible to exercise. Now a patient has a home facility and leaks a share of encounters to others: emergencies go wherever is nearest, oncology and cardiac referrals go to the specialist centre.",
    "p_out_of_network": 0.11,
